[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Sources:** [`INITIAL.md`](../INITIAL.md), [`PROJECT_BRIEF.md`](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md),
[stderr] +and [`01-game-identity.md`](01-game-identity.md). Labels are **explicit**
[stderr] +(direct request), **implied** (needed to fulfil it), **assumed** (reversible
[stderr] +guardrail), **deferred** (stated later scope), and **requires-decision**
[stderr] +(consequential unknown).
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## game-design-signals and module boundary
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Signal | Classification | Brief evidence |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Archetypes | Football trivia, puzzle, turn-based/card-like quiz; 2D single-player. | Creation statement and checked characteristics. |
[stderr] +| Primary activity | Recall/recognise, choose or enter, confirm, review football answers. | Themed rounds, formats, validation, feedback. |
[stderr] +| Session model | Short mobile-friendly themed rounds with save/resume. | Quick mobile sessions and local progress. |
[stderr] +| Knowledge source | Curated editorial first-release question bank. | Explicit bank requirement. |
[stderr] +| Competitive/cooperative model | Single-player; connected multiplayer unresolved. | Checked single-player; services named separately. |
[stderr] +| Creative intensity | Editorial trivia/feedback high; fictional narrative/world low. | Trivia focus versus generic campaign/battle text. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Selected candidates: question-bank/editorial QA, round/mode rules, answer
[stderr] +adjudication, scoring/streaks, anti-repetition, onboarding, progress/save,
[stderr] +accessible input/presentation, target delivery, original feedback assets,
[stderr] +release/content operations, and quality engineering. Rejected: RPG
[stderr] +world/party/boss/quest/combat/equipment; builder systems; racing or football
[stderr] +match simulation; platforming; and unapproved social play. Accounts,
[stderr] +multiplayer, live operations, and commerce are decision-gated, never selected
[stderr] +merely because common games include them.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Candidate system map
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Discipline / system family | Label | Rationale | Source reference |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Quiz shell, navigation, pause, lifecycle, results | implied | Quick playable rounds need entry, completion, exit, interruption. | Creation; quick mobile sessions |
[stderr] +| Round/theme/mode rules and local milestones | explicit | Themed rounds, playable loop, local progress. | Creation; required capabilities |
[stderr] +| Question schema: formats, categories, difficulty, answer rules, adjudication | explicit | Formats, validation, curated bank are direct. | Creation |
[stderr] +| Editorial workflow: provenance, fact review, correction, refresh | implied | Curated factual questions require accountable review/correction. | Curated question bank |
[stderr] +| Scores, streaks, feedback/explanations, anti-repetition | explicit | Scores/streaks/feedback named; repeat control enables variety. | Creation |
[stderr] +| Onboarding/tutorial and player guidance | explicit | Required capability. | Required first-release capabilities |
[stderr] +| Save/load/resume, persistence, migrations, data-loss recovery | explicit | Direct shared and first-release requirement. | Shared; required capabilities |
[stderr] +| Responsive 2D rendering, input adapters, browser performance | explicit | 2D, responsive web, keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad. | Characteristics; web requirements |
[stderr] +| PWA installation, offline assets/content, cache/update safety | explicit | Direct PWA requirement. | PWA requirements |
[stderr] +| Android/iOS packaging, touch/orientation, mobile budgets | explicit | Both targets named. | Android/iPhone requirements |
[stderr] +| Accessibility: controls, text, captions, visual settings, focus/reduced motion | explicit | Direct shared requirement. | Shared requirements |
[stderr] +| Localisation and language-content pipeline | explicit | Localisation named; languages unknown. | Cross-platform decisions |
[stderr] +| Original visual/audio feedback and asset pipeline | explicit | Feedback and art direction named. | Required capabilities; art direction |
[stderr] +| Content delivery/versioning/validation/rollback communication | implied | Curated content and updates need controlled release. | Content delivery; PWA requirements |
[stderr] +| Crash diagnostics, error boundaries, recovery UI, support triage | explicit | Crash reporting and player recovery are direct. | Shared; required capabilities |
[stderr] +| Quality: correctness, adjudication, persistence, offline/update, accessibility, compatibility, performance | implied | Each promise needs validation beyond screens. | Targets; shared requirements |
[stderr] +| Privacy/security, consent, minimisation, retention/deletion | explicit | Privacy required; accounts/diagnostics may process data. | Constraints; cross-platform decisions |
[stderr] +| Account identity, remote sync, conflicts | requires-decision | Named but no policy or local-state relationship. | Required capabilities; data policy |
