[stderr] +# 01 — Game identity
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Status:** first-release game layer, before genre-specific content planning.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Pillars and stable design units
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| ID | Unit | Commitment |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| GAME-001 | Fast football knowledge | Enter a themed trivia round and make repeated answer decisions in a quick mobile-friendly session. |
[stderr] +| GAME-002 | Fair, legible adjudication | Every question has an answer rule and communicates result, score change, and feedback accessibly. |
[stderr] +| GAME-003 | Momentum without punishment | Scores/streaks create tension; wrong answers are recoverable and results are understandable. |
[stderr] +| GAME-004 | Curated variety | Authored categories, formats, difficulty, and anti-repetition make short sessions fresh. |
[stderr] +| GAME-005 | Trustworthy return play | Local progress, save/resume, approved offline content, settings, and recovery support safe return. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Fantasy, loop, sessions, and progression
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Player fantasy: be the person who spots the football answer before the clock,
[stderr] +builds a run of confident calls, and improves their knowledge. Verbs: **read or
[stderr] +listen**, **recall**, **select or enter**, **confirm**, **review**, **continue**.
[stderr] +Loop: choose/receive theme → consume prompt → submit → adjudication and
[stderr] +accessible feedback → update score/streak/progress → next suitable prompt →
[stderr] +finish or safely resume. Sessions are short, interruptible rounds with
[stderr] +onboarding first, an objective, question sequence, results, and saved return
[stderr] +state. Progression promises broader knowledge and local milestones, not levels,
[stderr] +equipment, traversal, or combat power.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The emotional arc is curiosity, competence, mounting stakes, then celebration
[stderr] +or useful recovery. Audience: casual adult football-interested players using
[stderr] +touch, keyboard, mouse, gamepad, captions, adjustable text, and visual settings.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## game-design-signals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Signal | Classification and evidence | Design consequence |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Archetype | Football trivia/puzzle/turn-based card-like quiz; source names trivia, formats, and checked puzzle/card/board/turn-based. | Questions, rounds, answers, and results—not action/adventure content. |
[stderr] +| Primary activity | Recall/recognise and answer; source names validation and feedback. | Input, adjudication, explanations, and score rules. |
[stderr] +| Session model | Quick mobile sessions with local progress/save. | Short lifecycle and interruption-safe state. |
[stderr] +| Knowledge source | Curated editorial football bank. | Provenance, review, categories, difficulty, refresh. |
[stderr] +| Social model | Single-player; multiplayer is undefined. | No opponents, matchmaking, chat, co-op, rankings, or social graph in core. |
[stderr] +| Creative intensity | Editorial questions/feedback high; fictional narrative low. | Question tooling, not lore/character pipeline. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Candidate module decision record
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Module | Decision | Rationale |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Question provenance/categories/formats/difficulty/answers/explanations | Selected | Necessary for curated themed trivia and validation. |
[stderr] +| Round/mode rules, scoring/streaks, results, anti-repetition, milestones | Selected | Named or necessary for replayable short sessions. |
[stderr] +| Onboarding, accessibility, input, save/recovery, web/PWA/mobile delivery | Selected | Explicit shared and target requirements. |
[stderr] +| Editorial refresh and validation tooling | Selected candidate | Factual curated content needs correction and quality controls; cadence awaits approval. |
[stderr] +| Accounts/sync, multiplayer safety, live ops, commerce | Requires decision | Named but conflicts with core and lacks policy. |
[stderr] +| RPG world/party/quests/combat/jobs/enemies/bosses/equipment/locations | Rejected | Not evidenced; generic campaign/battle wording is a decision, not scope. |
[stderr] +| Builder economy/construction; racing physics; match simulation; platforming | Rejected | No player-activity evidence. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Completion is an accessible results state with score, streak outcome, and next
[stderr] +step; an interruption becomes safe resumable state where supported. Narrative,
[stderr] +competitive-rank, and seasonal completion are outside first release unless an
[stderr] +approval decision changes this identity.
